From c7c301790f7cb7e179ff4d268fdbfc867ddac07d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:26:43 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_updates: Form page with a titled "System updates" section

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). Settings, kcfg keys and behaviour unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- Kirigami.Form/FormGroup/FormEntry -> Kirigami.FormLayout (same as the other reworked pages).
- Section 1 (untitled): Update software: Manually / Automatically (+ help button), frequency combo.
- New section "System updates" holds the apply choice; "Apply system updates:" -> "Apply updates:"
  (kcm_updates/useOfflineUpdates). Section and rows stay hidden when a reboot is mandatory
  (kcm_updates/MandatoryReboot); immutable still disables them.
- "Recommended to maximize system stability" is now a small hint label under "After rebooting".
- All 5 inventory rows kept, 0 lost (inventory/relabel/kcm_updates.tsv in the outer repo).

Speed: the page reads only two KConfig skeletons (updates.cpp has no D-Bus/PackageKit at load), so there is
nothing to defer; the QML is smaller than before. After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-013, HIG-017, HIG-019, HIG-020.

Not built yet. Kirigami.FormLayout, ContextualHelpButton, SettingStateBinding are all used by other pages in master.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
